<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-RAIN HALTS ZIMBABWE/INDIA MATCH.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-RAIN HALTS ZIMBABWE/INDIA MATCH.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heavy rain prevented the resumption of the day/night match between India and Zimbabwe at Centurion Park.</p>
<p>India scored 216 all out in 48.4 of their 50 over allocation, but Zimbabwe's reply was stymied by the rain which began to fall during the break.</p>
<p>The umpires were to make a decision at 2135 local (1935 gmt). If 25 overs of the second innings could not be bowled a new match will begin on Saturday.</p>
